            <ArticleTitle>[Differential diagnosis of groin pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2882-4, 2886-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Groin pain is frequent but often problematic as it covers a very broad differential diagnosis. The localisation of pain in one of the five anterior hip regions helps to establish a precise diagnosis and an adapted treatment. We review the differential diagnosis and treatment of anterior hip pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
